    <description>Stamps the line-level Description from the source order line onto the Asset for every lifecycle event (Initial Sale, Upsells/amendments, Renewals). Triggers on AssetAction creation (each lifecycle event creates exactly one AssetAction) and runs on the async-after-commit path so the source OrderItem.Description has settled. Resolves the described line by looping the AssetAction&apos;s sources: each AssetActionSource.ReferenceEntityItemId is tried as an OrderItem directly, and if it is instead an OrderItemDetail (as happens on many amendments/renewals, which carry no Description of their own) it hops OrderItemDetail.OrderItemId to the parent OrderItem. Writes the writable Asset.Description (Asset.ProductDescription is a system-locked mirror of Product2.Description). Only writes when a non-blank description is found, so a description-less line can never blank out an existing value. Supersedes Fortra_Asset_Stamp_Line_Description (Asset-Create-triggered), which only fired at asset birth and could not resolve OrderItemDetail sources.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Fortra | AssetAction | Stamp Line Description {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Fortra | AssetAction | Stamp Line Description</label>
